---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import cities from '../../data/cities.json';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Website Audit', href: '/website-audit/' },
  { label: 'Services', href: '/website-audit-services/' },
  { label: 'Locations', href: '/website-audit-services/locations/' },
];

const toc = [
  { label: 'How Remote Audits Work', id: 'remote-audits' },
  { label: 'UK Service Areas', id: 'uk-locations' },
  { label: 'US Service Areas', id: 'us-locations' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Remote Website Audit Services by Location',
  provider: { '@type': 'Organization', '@id': 'https://auditweb.site/#organization', name: 'AuditWeb', url: 'https://auditweb.site/' },
  description: 'Remote website audit services available to organisations across listed UK and US locations.',
  areaServed: [...cities.uk.map(c => c.name), ...cities.us.map(c => c.name)],
};
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Remote Website Audit Services by Location"
  description="Browse UK and US service areas for AuditWeb's remote website audits. Each engagement uses a written scope, dated evidence and USD pricing from $297."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  schema={schema}
  publishDate="2026-08-26"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>

<p>AuditWeb delivers website audits remotely to organisations in the UK and US service areas listed below. The city pages describe availability and scoping. They do not represent local offices or claim local audit evidence.</p>

<h2 id="remote-audits">How do remote website audits work?</h2>
<p>Each engagement starts with the website, business question, priority pages and available data. A city can define which landing pages and named competitors enter the scope. Findings still require dated evidence from the site or agreed data sources.</p>
<p>Basic audits start at $297 USD and comprehensive audits start at $997 USD. Read the <a href="/website-audit-services/">website audit service</a> page for deliverables, scope limits and custom-quote cases.</p>

<h2 id="uk-locations">Which UK locations can request a remote audit?</h2>
<ul>
  {cities.uk.map(city => (
    <li><a href={`/website-audit-services/${city.slug}/`}>{city.name}</a> — {city.region}</li>
  ))}
</ul>

<h2 id="us-locations">Which US locations can request a remote audit?</h2>
<ul>
  {cities.us.map(city => (
    <li><a href={`/website-audit-services/${city.slug}/`}>{city.name}</a> — {city.region}</li>
  ))}
</ul>

<p>Do not see your city listed? Use the main service enquiry to ask about remote coverage. Include your site URL, location, priority pages and audit question so AuditWeb can confirm scope.</p>

</ContentLayout>
